layout: layouts/base.njk
title: "Download & install"
description: "How Ferrite is installed on the Radtel RT-950 Pro (and radios built on the same hardware), and how to check a release's signature."
---
<div class="wrap column download">
  <header class="page-head">
    <h1>Download</h1>
  </header>

  {% if not site.release.released %}
  <div class="callout">
    <p><b>Coming soon.</b> Follow the <a href="{{ site.urls.blog }}/">blog</a> or the
      <a href="{{ site.discord }}">Discord</a> to hear when it's ready.</p>
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  <div class="prose">
    <h3>What you need</h3>
    <p>A Radtel RT-950 Pro, or a radio built on the same hardware, its programming cable, and Chrome, Edge or
      Firefox on a computer. Keep the stock firmware file (the <code>.BTF</code>): it's your way back.</p>

    <h3>Installing</h3>
    <p>In <a href="{{ site.urls.console }}">Ferrite Console</a>:</p>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li><b>Connect</b> the cable and turn the radio on.</li>
      <li><b>Back up</b> the whole radio. Console won't install until the backup is saved.</li>
      <li><b>Install.</b> Drop in your stock <code>.BTF</code> for SSB, optional.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Your calibration is never erased. Channels can come back from a CHIRP CSV.</p>

    <h3>Going back to stock</h3>
    <p>The same page in Console writes your backup back, then the original firmware, and the radio is as it was.</p>

    <h3>Checking a release</h3>
    <p>Every release is signed with <a href="https://jedisct1.github.io/minisign/">minisign</a>, and Console checks
      it before installing.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="keybox"><small>Ferrite's public key · ID {{ site.minisign.id }}</small>{{ site.minisign.key }}</div>
  <pre class="wrapcode"><code>minisign -Vm ferrite.btf -P {{ site.minisign.key }}</code></pre>

  <div class="prose">
    <h3>Updating</h3>
    <p>Console's Firmware Update keeps your channels and settings; the <a href="{{ site.urls.manual }}">user guide</a>
      has the steps.</p>

    <h3>Help</h3>
    <p>Stuck, or something not right? Ask on the <a href="{{ site.discord }}">Ferrite Discord</a>.</p>
  </div>
</div>
